**Fixed in #752** (merge 8277233f85).

`git config --global …` is now recognised as a write of `~/.gitconfig`. It gets the #620 treatment: no Grant once, and the prompt and denial say it is a start-up file outside the current folder that can't be granted, not even once. The test is `issue_736_740.rs::issue_737_git_config_global_is_offered_no_grant` (real sandbox, macOS and glitch). It fails before the fix and passes after.

The same detection now covers:
- `git config --system`, `--file` and the repository's `.git/config`;
- `npm config set|delete|edit` and `npm set` (`~/.npmrc`, `--userconfig`, `--location=project`);
- `pip config set|unset|edit`;
- `gh config set`.

Reads aren't treated as writes: `--get`, `--list`, `get`, or a key on its own. Config files outside the folder that aren't start-up files get a new explanation that the file is outside the current folder.

**Evidence:** tmux replay `qa/security-levels/fixes/issue-736-740-20261014/` (prompt without Grant once, denial explained), [video](https://github.com/CorbanuCore/CorbanuTerminal/releases/download/demos/issue-737-issue737-gitconfig-no-grant-a79ff79b392a-2026-10-13.mp4).
